{title: Here I Am}
{artist: Dionne Stratton}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 123}

{c: Intro}

{c: Verse 1}
Your Spirit whispers
"Come away with Me"
Your presence lingers
Beyond what I can see
Lord, You are the life
Sustaining my soul
You breathe into me
And I am made whole

{c: Chorus}
So here I am
With an open heart
I welcome You 
And all that You are
Your life is a spring
Welling up in me
And all for Your glory
Jesus, I receive
So here I am

{c: Verse 2}
Bread that came from heaven
Once broken for me
Blood that flowed like water
Grace that set me free
You call me Your own
Lord, teach me to abide
You've made me Your home
Your Spirit lives inside

{c: Chorus}
So here I am
With an open heart
I welcome You 
And all that You are
Your life is a spring
Welling up in me
And all for Your glory
Jesus, I receive
So here I am

{c: Bridge}
Lord of all creation
Love that took my debt
You are the resurrection
Life that conquers death
Now my life is hidden in You
Your scars the living proof

{c: Chorus}
So here I am
With an open heart
I welcome You  
And all that You are
Your life is a spring
Welling up in me
And all for Your glory
Jesus, I receive...

{c: Chorus}
So here I am
With an open heart
I welcome You 
And all that You are
Your life is a spring
Welling up in me
And all for Your glory
Jesus, I receive
So here I am

{c: Outro}
I want to pour out for You
A holy offering
My life hidden in You
And what You did for me
But first let me receive...

So here I am...
Here I am
